Package: pcountr
Title: Read, Convert, and Analyse Pollen Counts from PCount and Modern Formats
Version: 0.5.1
Authors@R:
    person("William", "Nanavati",
           email   = "william.nanavati@umontana.edu",
           role    = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = ""))
Description: Reads legacy MS-DOS 'PCount' pollen-count files (.CNT) and their
    dictionaries (.DIC), converting them into a tidy, self-contained native
    format (YAML) that additionally carries sample depth and (optional) age.
    Reproduces PCount's report calculations (pollen sums, tracer-spike ratios,
    grain concentrations, traverse statistics and preservation tabulations) and
    provides export helpers for downstream stratigraphic plotting (e.g. 'rioja')
    and statistical analysis. Chronology construction itself is delegated to
    dedicated tools (e.g. 'rbacon', 'clam', 'neotoma2'); pcountr only performs
    accumulation-rate arithmetic from analyst-supplied ages.
    Dedicated to the memory of Dr. Eric C. Grimm (1951--2020), who developed
    PCount at the Illinois State Museum and trained generations of palynologists
    in its use.
